# JAMAL MULTI-SYSTEM MANAGEMENT
## Customer Service & Automated Notification Management System

### 1. Introduction

The Customer Service & Automated Notification Management System is a feature that will be integrated into Jamal Multi-System Management.

Its purpose is to allow Jamal to automatically monitor activities happening across different modules, identify important events and notify the relevant users without requiring manual intervention.

The main idea is that **Jamal should be intelligent enough to identify when something requires attention and automatically communicate that information to the responsible user.**

For example:
- When stock reaches its minimum level, notify the business owner.
- When stock runs out, send an urgent notification.
- When a payment is received, notify the responsible user.
- When an invoice becomes overdue, notify the responsible user.
- When a subscription is about to expire, notify the account owner.

---

### 2. How the System Will Work

The notification system will operate internally within Jamal.

It will have four major responsibilities:

**A. Event Monitoring**

The system monitors activities across all Jamal modules.

Examples:
- Stock management.
- Sales management.
- Purchase management.
- Financial management.
- Employee management.
- Customer management.
- Subscription management.

**B. Condition Checking**

Whenever an activity occurs, Jamal checks whether it meets a predefined notification condition.

For example:

A business has 10 packets of socks.

The owner establishes a minimum stock level of 3 packets.

Whenever a sale occurs, Jamal updates the stock quantity and checks whether the remaining quantity has reached the minimum level.

**C. Notification Generation**

When a condition is met, Jamal automatically generates an appropriate notification message.

**D. Notification Delivery**

Jamal delivers the notification through the available communication channels.

---

### 3. Stock Management Example

Suppose the initial stock is 10 packets.

The owner sets the minimum stock level to 3 packets.

| Event | Available stock | System response |
|---|---:|---|
| Initial stock | 10 | No notification |
| Sale | 7 | No notification |
| Sale | 5 | No notification |
| Sale | 4 | No notification |
| Sale | 3 | Low-stock notification |
| Sale | 2 | Critical-stock notification |
| Sale | 0 | Out-of-stock notification |

When stock reaches 3 packets, Jamal generates:

**Notification:**

"LOW STOCK ALERT: Your Socks stock has reached its minimum level of 3 packets. Please restock."

The notification can appear on the owner's dashboard and, if SMS is enabled, be sent to their registered phone number.

---

### 4. Internal Notification Engine

Jamal should have its own notification engine responsible for managing notifications across the entire system.

The engine should handle:

1. Detecting events.
2. Checking notification conditions.
3. Identifying the recipient.
4. Generating messages.
5. Selecting the delivery channel.
6. Sending notifications.
7. Recording notification history.
8. Tracking delivery status where supported.

This engine should be reusable across all modules rather than implementing separate notification systems for every module.

---

### 5. Notification Channels

Jamal should support multiple communication channels.

| Channel | Description | External service required? |
|---|---|---|
| In-app notification | Displays alerts inside Jamal | No |
| Dashboard notification | Displays important alerts on the dashboard | No |
| SMS | Sends messages to phone numbers | Yes |
| Email | Sends notifications to email addresses | Yes |
| Push notification | Sends alerts to mobile devices or supported browsers | Usually requires a push service |

**Important distinction:**

Jamal can independently generate, manage, store and display notifications.

However, sending ordinary SMS messages to mobile phone numbers requires access to an SMS gateway or mobile network infrastructure.

For Tanzania, Africa's Talking is one possible SMS provider.

---

### 6. Notification Settings

Every business owner should have control over notification preferences.

For example:

| Setting | Owner's choice |
|---|---|
| Low-stock notification | Enabled |
| Out-of-stock notification | Enabled |
| Payment notification | Enabled |
| Overdue invoice notification | Enabled |
| SMS notification | Enabled |
| Email notification | Disabled |
| Dashboard notification | Enabled |

The owner should also be able to configure minimum stock levels for individual products.

---

### 7. Notification History

Jamal should maintain a notification history containing:

- Notification title.
- Notification message.
- Related module.
- Recipient.
- Date and time.
- Notification channel.
- Delivery status.
- Read/unread status.

This allows users to review previous notifications.

---

### 8. Important Technical Requirements

The notification engine should:

- Operate automatically in the background.
- Avoid sending duplicate notifications for the same event.
- Support multiple businesses and organizations.
- Respect user permissions.
- Support different notification preferences.
- Handle failed SMS or email delivery.
- Maintain notification records.
- Process notifications efficiently without slowing down the main system.

For stock notifications, Jamal should detect when stock crosses the minimum threshold rather than repeatedly sending the same alert every time the stock is updated.

For example, if the minimum is 3 and stock reaches 3, send an alert once. If stock is replenished to 10 and later drops to 3 again, send a new alert.

---

## 9. Proposed System Architecture

The architecture should look like this:

```text
       JAMAL MULTI-SYSTEM MANAGEMENT
                    |
          DIFFERENT SYSTEM MODULES
                    |
     +--------------+--------------+
     |              |              |
   STOCK           SALES         FINANCE
     |              |              |
     +--------------+--------------+
                    |
             EVENT DETECTION
                    |
           NOTIFICATION ENGINE
                    |
          CONDITION VERIFICATION
                    |
           MESSAGE GENERATION
                    |
            DELIVERY MANAGER
                    |
       +------------+------------+
       |            |            |
     IN-APP         SMS         EMAIL
       |            |            |
       |       SMS GATEWAY   EMAIL SERVICE
       |            |            |
       +------------+------------+
                    |
             NOTIFICATION LOGS
```

---

## 10. Final Objective

The goal is to make Jamal a proactive management system rather than a system that only waits for users to open different modules and check information manually.

Jamal should be able to:

- Monitor business activities.
- Recognize important events.
- Identify problems before they become serious.
- Automatically notify responsible users.
- Maintain communication records.
- Help business owners make timely decisions.

**My architectural recommendation:** Build one centralized Notification Engine inside Jamal that serves every module. Do not build separate notification engines for Stock, Sales, Finance and other modules. External services should only be used when communication must happen outside Jamal, such as SMS and email.